Retail Business Performance & Profitability Analysis Report

Abstract

This project utilizes real-world retail transaction data to identify and analyze key operational inefficiencies, focusing primarily on profitability and inventory turnover. By integrating SQL for robust data aggregation and Python for statistical analysis, we established a quantitative link between Shipping Lead Time (as a proxy for inventory days) and Profit Margin. The analysis successfully pinpointed high-risk product categories—those characterized by both low profit margins and extended fulfillment times—providing the foundation for immediate strategic interventions in inventory management and pricing. The final deliverable is a comprehensive plan for an interactive BI dashboard to monitor these metrics in real-time.

1. Introduction and Objectives

The success of any retail operation hinges on efficiently managing both costs and inventory flow. Profitability can be unknowingly eroded by slow-moving stock that incurs high carrying costs or by products that require excessive time to fulfill, leading to increased logistics expenditure and customer dissatisfaction.

The primary objectives of this project were to:

Calculate accurate profit margins at the Category and Sub-Category levels.

Quantify the relationship between inventory efficiency and profitability using correlation analysis.

Identify specific profit-draining categories requiring urgent managerial action.

Design a robust BI dashboard layout for continuous performance monitoring.

